DECREE UNDER SECTION 36 OF THE ARBITRATION AND CONCILIATION ACT, 1996

IN THE HIGH COURT OF RAJASTHAN AT JODHPUR
ARBITRATION APPEAL NO. _______ / 2023

IN THE MATTER OF:
ARBITRAL AWARD DATED 30.11.2023
PASSED BY THREE-MEMBER ARBITRAL TRIBUNAL
PRESIDING ARBITRATOR: JUSTICE (RETD.) S.K. SINGH

BETWEEN:
M/s. Roadcon Infra Pvt. Ltd., Jaipur                  ...Decree Holder
AND
National Highways Authority of India (NHAI)          ...Judgment Debtor

DECREE

THIS HON'BLE COURT, after hearing the arguments of both parties and perusing the Arbitral Award dated 30.11.2023, hereby:

1. CONFIRMS AND MAKES RULE the Arbitral Award dated 30.11.2023 as a decree of this Court under Section 36 of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996.

2. DECLARES that the Judgment Debtor (NHAI) shall pay to the Decree Holder (M/s. Roadcon Infra Pvt. Ltd.) a sum of ₹23,01,00,000 (Rupees Twenty-Three Crore One Lakh only) along with interest @ 12% per annum from 01.03.2022 till realization.

3. DIRECTS the Judgment Debtor to:
   a) Release the Security Deposit of ₹1.12 Crore within 30 days from the date of this decree.
   b) Release the Performance Guarantee of ₹5.63 Crore within 30 days from the date of this decree.
   c) Pay the costs of arbitration proceedings amounting to ₹15,50,000 within 30 days.

4. DECLARES that the termination of contract dated 01.06.2022 is illegal and void ab initio.

5. GRANTS Extension of Time of 450 days as awarded by the Arbitral Tribunal.

6. REJECTS the Application for Stay of Execution filed by NHAI under Section 36(3) of the Arbitration Act, the same being without merit.

7. DIRECTS the Judgment Debtor to deposit 75% of the awarded amount (₹17.26 Crore) in this Court within 45 days as a condition for any future appeal, failing which the decree shall be executable in entirety.

8. AWARDS costs of this proceeding to the Decree Holder.

GIVEN under the seal and signature of this Hon'ble Court on this ___ day of ________, 2023.

Sd/-
JUDGE
HIGH COURT OF RAJASTHAN, JODHPUR